# Optional overrides: Foundry needs none of them. To set one, copy this file
# to local/.env (Compose reads it whether it runs from the repository's root
# or from local/), uncomment it, and run docker compose up -d again. An empty
# value is the default. local/README.md says more of each.
#
# No secrets go here: the first start writes them into the `secrets` volume.
# An install set up before with setup.sh keeps its FOUNDRY_LOCAL_TOKEN,
# FOUNDRY_S3_SECRET, FOUNDRY_MYSQL_PASSWORD and FOUNDRY_CONNECTOR_KEY in this
# file: its first start copies them into the volume, and they stay used.

# The install's AI provider. Unset, Foundry finds one: Claude on the
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, else OpenAI on the OPENAI_API_KEY, of the shell that ran
# docker compose; else an Ollama with a model that calls tools; else LM
# Studio on this computer. none: no provider until an owner chooses one in
# Settings › AI models. Else anthropic, openai, ollama, openai_compatible,
# azure_openai or bedrock, with the fields its kind takes.
# FOUNDRY_AI_PROVIDER=
# FOUNDRY_AI_API_KEY=
# FOUNDRY_AI_BASE_URL=
# FOUNDRY_AI_API=
# FOUNDRY_AI_REGION=
# FOUNDRY_AI_ENDPOINT=
# FOUNDRY_AI_CONTEXT_TOKENS=
# A model for every task, or one per task (each wins over FOUNDRY_AI_MODEL).
# FOUNDRY_AI_MODEL=
# FOUNDRY_AI_DRAFT_MODEL=
# FOUNDRY_AI_ASK_MODEL=
# FOUNDRY_AI_EXTRACT_MODEL=
# FOUNDRY_AI_VERIFY_MODEL=

# Ollama in Docker (docker compose --profile ollama up -d): the model it
# pulls, and the digest it must be, when set.
# FOUNDRY_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b
# FOUNDRY_OLLAMA_DIGEST=

# Images other than the release's, such as ones built from this checkout
# with docker compose build.
# FOUNDRY_SITE_IMAGE=helix-foundry/site:local
# FOUNDRY_IMAGE=helix-foundry/foundry:local
# FOUNDRY_AGENT_IMAGE=
